//avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86391540?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/googs1025","html_url":"https://github.com/googs1025","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/googs1025/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/googs1025/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/googs1025/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/googs1025/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/googs1025/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/googs1025/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/googs1025/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/googs1025/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/googs1025/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T12:10:19Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T12:11:24Z","body":"Are there any real scenarios for this? Initial thoughts: Why is this configuration necessary? Would it be a good configuration option if possible? Is it easy and quick for users to understand? Additionally, my two cents:  modify the \"event content\" rather than the \"configuration length\". We should aim to describe preblem using more concise logs rather than endlessly increasing length. 🤔 ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/2470367857/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/2470641248","html_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/128747#issuecomment-2470641248","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/128747","id":2470641248,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAToIks6TQv5g","user":{"login":"jmelton-cw","id":186602289,"node_id":"U_kgDOCx9TMQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186602289?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw","html_url":"https://github.com/jmelton-cw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T14:11:12Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T14:11:12Z","body":"This is a fair point about the content of the message being formed more concisely rather than arbitrarily increasing note size.\r\n\r\nThe scenario I've encountered primarily is endlessly long lists of nodes with taints that are preventing pod scheduling which I think was similar to the message being created in that original bug. \r\n\r\nIn this scenario we have taints that are used to mark nodes for reserved capacity, the taint key is shared (\"our.org.taint/reserved:<orgid-string>\" as an example) but all the values are unique based on an org-id which generates many hundreds of unique taint messages as we have many orgs. If there was some way to maybe condense messages enumerating taints with the same key along the lines of `(X) node(s) had taint key {our.org.tain/reserved} and (Y) unique values`, it could make messages concise enough for the other contents of the message that might also be preventing scheduling to show up as well (there are other scheduling related issues making the pod unschedulable besides reservation taints but they are just clobbered by the extensive list of reserved taints and it never makes it into the event)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/2470641248/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/2475865402","html_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/128747#issuecomment-2475865402","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/128747","id":2475865402,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAToIks6TkrU6","user":{"login":"sftim","id":22591623,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTkxNjIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22591623?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sftim","html_url":"https://github.com/sftim","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sftim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sftim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sftim/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sftim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sftim/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sftim/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sftim/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sftim/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sftim/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T09:42:51Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T09:42:51Z","body":"- This might need a KEP; the problem is that the Event API is part of conformance. Imagine if many clusters set the note length to 10KiB but some use the upstream minimum of 1KB, and then software in the ecosystem expects to be able to use 10KiB notes.\r\n\r\n- We could define an out-of-tree but standardized API, eg EventContext, that provides\r\n  - space for additional detail\r\n  - unstructured storage for additional context\r\n  - an unambiguous, field-selectable reference to the associated event\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThere is a wider pattern here I advocate for: core Kubernetes being aware of extension APIs. We already do this for CSI, a little. For example, the kube-controller-manager could use discovery to either:\r\n\r\n1. notice that there is no EventContext API present, and therefore take no special action\r\n2. notice that there is an EventContext API present, at a compatible API version, and therefore garbage collect EventContexts as the associated Events disappear (maybe using a watch that only reports deletes? I'm thinking out loud)\r\n\r\nI favor making the smallest in-tree change that enables us to provide value to users. Even if some in-tree change is needed, keeping the core of Kubernetes lean helps us ensure it's maintainable.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/2475865402/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/2479038055","html_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/128747#issuecomment-2479038055","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/128747","id":2479038055,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAToIks6Twx5n","user":{"login":"jmelton-cw","id":186602289,"node_id":"U_kgDOCx9TMQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186602289?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw","html_url":"https://github.com/jmelton-cw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmelton-cw/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T14:39:34Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T14:39:34Z","body":"If a KEP would be appropriate for this and a different solution than a simple configurable note size is more appropriate I can try and put something together. I'll be honest that I'm not a developer and generally I am just looking for some better observability into issues that I encounter in my work, and having truncated event messages was frustrating.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/2479038055/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/2656904321","html_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/128747#issuecomment-2656904321","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/128747","id":2656904321,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAToIks6eXSSB","user":{"login":"k8s-triage-robot","id":53270907,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMjcwOTA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53270907?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/k8s-triage-robot","html_url":"https://github.com/k8s-triage-robot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k8s-triage-robot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k8s-triage-robot/following{/other_u